{"book":11,"chapter":29,"rubric":"MODERN FRONTEND / JAVASCRIPT IN NODE.JS / CHAPTER 21","slides":[{"title":"JavaScript outside the browser","sub":"Chapter 29 · Node.js","short":"Intro","main":"You need to understand how Node is built.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Outside the browser","Chapter plan","Exercises"],"captions":["Node.js is JavaScript on the server, on the command line and in the tools we use every day","How the runtime is built, V8 and libuv, the event loop phases, the thread pool, modules, parallel processes, exit codes and graceful shutdown","In the exercises we build models of the event loop, the module loader, the garbage collector and a restart manager"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":40.0,"text":"browser","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Node.js","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":66.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"V8","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"libuv","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":294.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"loop","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":66.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"modules","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"processes","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t5","x":294.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"shutdown","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["createLoop()","resolveModule(req, dir)","createHeap().collect()","createSupervisor(opts)"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[13.1,33.2]}]},{"title":"Node layers","sub":"V8, libuv, bindings","short":"Layers","main":"One main thread for your code.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["V8 and libuv","Bindings and modules","One thread for code"],"captions":["At the bottom, V8 is the engine that parses and runs code, and libuv is a cross-platform C library for I/O and the event loop","Between them sit C++ bindings and built-in modules: files, network, streams, processes, crypto; instead of window there are process and globalThis","Your code runs in one main thread; Node delegates blocking work"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":40.0,"w":240.0,"h":30.0,"text":"V8 (JavaScript)","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":240.0,"h":30.0,"text":"libuv (I/O, loop)","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":30.0,"w":240.0,"h":24.0,"text":"fs · net · http · stream · crypto","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":240.0,"h":24.0,"text":"C++ bindings","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"w":240.0,"h":24.0,"text":"V8 + libuv","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":40.0,"text":"main thread: JS","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":24.0,"text":"thread pool","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":270.0,"y":90.0,"w":110.0,"h":24.0,"text":"OS async I/O","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":56.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":150.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":214.0,"y2":90.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[13.7,21.1]}]},{"title":"V8","sub":"JIT, shapes, GC","short":"V8","main":"Stable shapes are faster.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Bytecode and JIT","Hidden classes","Garbage collection"],"captions":["The parser builds a tree, the Ignition interpreter runs bytecode and collects statistics, hot functions are compiled by an optimizing compiler; a wrong guess means deoptimization","Objects with the same property order share a hidden shape; the inline cache remembers shapes, so stable shapes are faster","Generational GC: the young generation is cleaned often and fast, survivors move to the old one, which is visited less often"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s0","x":66.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"AST","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s1","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"bytecode","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s2","x":294.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"machine","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"hot code → optimization","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["{ x, y }  → form A","{ y, x }  → form B","","f(p) { return p.x }  // needs 1 shape type"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"js","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"y","x":100.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":44.0,"text":"young: often","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":260.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":44.0,"text":"old: rarely","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":156.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":204.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[12.5,32.9]}]},{"title":"Loop phases","sub":"timers → poll → check","short":"Loop","main":"The loop ends when there is no work left.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Phases","Poll and check","Exit"],"captions":["The loop goes round and round: timers → pending callbacks → idle/prepare → poll → check → close callbacks","In poll the loop receives I/O events and waits for them if needed; check runs setImmediate","While there are active handles and tasks, the loop keeps going; when none are left, the process exits by itself"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"p0","x":66.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"timers","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p1","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pending","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p2","x":294.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"idle","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p3","x":66.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"poll","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p4","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"check","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p5","x":294.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"close","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p0","x":66.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"timers","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p1","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pending","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p2","x":294.0,"y":56.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"idle","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p3","x":66.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"poll","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p4","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"check","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p5","x":294.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":28.0,"text":"close","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"no handles","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":154.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"exit","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.8,27.9]}]},{"title":"nextTick and microtasks","sub":"Queue order","short":"Queues","main":"Recursive nextTick starves the loop.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Two queues","Immediate and timeout","Starvation"],"captions":["After every callback the process.nextTick queue is drained first, then the microtask queue; this repeats until both are empty","setImmediate fires in the check phase; inside an I/O handler it always comes before setTimeout(…, 0)","Recursion through nextTick starves the loop: I/O never gets a turn"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"nextTick","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"promise.then","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":154.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"then — the next callback","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["fs.readFile(f, () => {","  setTimeout(() => log('T'), 0);","  setImmediate(() => log('I'));","});  // I, then T"],"hl":[2],"lang":"js","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["function loop() {","  process.nextTick(loop);","}  // I/O waits forever"],"hl":[1],"lang":"js","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[13.8,28.9]}]},{"title":"Thread pool","sub":"libuv thread pool","short":"Pool","main":"Don't block the main thread.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["What's in the pool","Size","Don't block"],"captions":["Sockets use kernel mechanisms (epoll, kqueue), while files, DNS lookup, zlib and part of crypto run in the libuv thread pool","By default the pool has four threads (UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE); with many tasks they queue up","Never block the main thread with long synchronous calls or computations — it freezes all requests"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":66.0,"y":70.0,"w":68.0,"h":32.0,"text":"fs","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":142.0,"y":70.0,"w":68.0,"h":32.0,"text":"dns.lookup","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":218.0,"y":70.0,"w":68.0,"h":32.0,"text":"zlib","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":294.0,"y":70.0,"w":68.0,"h":32.0,"text":"crypto","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size"